  "solution": {
    "text": "Volume of cylindrical wire, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is the diameter of wire.<br />Differentiating both sides,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>dV</mi><mi>dx</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>xL</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8901;</mo><mfrac><mi>dL</mi><mi>dx</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Also, volume remains constant<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>dV</mi><mi>dx</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>xL</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mi>dL</mi><mi>dx</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#10233;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>xL</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mi>dL</mi><mi>dx</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#10233;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mi>dx</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mi>dL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />Poisson&#39;s ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>"
